      "old_content": "<!-- wp:table -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td><strong>DR. SUN'S CLINICAL PERSPECTIVE</strong><em>\"children are frequently seen after years of being told their swelling is just how they are built, or that they are overweight, or that it will settle down. The delay matters because the earlier we start proper management, the better we can protect the tissues from the fibrotic changes that make lymphedema harder to treat over time.\"</em><em>This means for patients that if your instinct as a parent tells you that something is wrong with your child's limb, pursuing a specialist opinion is the right call, even if you have already been reassured by a general doctor. A diagnosis changes what is possible.</em></td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n<!-- /wp:table -->",
